      "simplifications": [
        "Every recommendation source in the live engine is replayed at each as-of point using only data dated on or before that point: hard-time rules, the survival model, lot defects, repeat snags and repeat NFF, engine trend flags, the oil precursor and fatigue. The pattern detectors are mirrored in backtest.py (the production detectors read the whole data set) and a test checks each mirror reproduces the production detector exactly at 15 Nov 2026.",
        "Coverage: a unit-level recommendation covers a failure of that same unit. A repeat-snag recommendation covers a failure of the recommended component's part number on that aircraft (any position), because it directs engineers at that system rather than at one serial. Fatigue recommendations are aircraft tasking reviews: they count towards the alert rate but cannot cover a component failure.",
        "As in production, a repeat-snag cluster stays a trigger once it has occurred (the detector looks at the full snag history up to the as-of date), and the oil precursor rule covers the fighter's lube oil pump.",
        "Alerts are evaluated at monthly as-of points (the 15th of each month from 15 Nov 2025 to 15 Oct 2026). An alert stays open until the unit is removed. The alert rate counts distinct Medium or higher recommendation episodes per source; as in production, a unit covered by a lot recommendation does not also get a survival recommendation.",
        "The tau trade-off table is analysis only: it re-runs the survival source at multiples of the section 6 thresholds. Production thresholds are unchanged.",
        "Model alerts follow the live queue: urgency bands U1 to U3, priority from the section 6 matrix, so a U3 flight-safety item is Medium and a U3 mission item is Low. Hard-time alerts use bands U1 to U3. Only Medium or higher counts.",
        "Tyres and brakes are excluded from every metric, as they are from the live recommendation queue (routine wear consumables, not failures to predict).",
        "Units installed during the test window start at zero FH with covariates taken from their aircraft's flying over the 365 days before installation.",
        "Exposure uses the production definition (gold unit_exposure.csv): hours flown inside the data window in the part's life basis (APU hours for APUs, FH otherwise) plus the time since new carried on the history card for units already fitted when the window opens. As in production, the survival fit conditions those units on their age at the window start (delayed entry)."
      ]
    },
